# What `vercel deploy` (the CLI) must not upload. Git deploys build from the
# repository, where none of these exist except .env.example, which no build
# reads — so this file only changes CLI deploys.
#
# The CLI does NOT read .gitignore: without this file it uploads everything
# except a short built-in list (.git, .next, node_modules, .env.local,
# .env.*.local, ...). That would ship a stale `out/` export (33 MB) and any
# `.env` or `.env.production` file someone creates later. Checked against the
# CLI 58 source and `vercel deploy --dry --json`, 2026-10-05.
out
.claude
.env*
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
